{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 42, :comments ["<b>A night of shemarim it is for YHWH.</b> For He guarded them from the destroyer when He struck Egypt; therefore HaShem commanded that it also be for Israel a night of shemurim for all generations — that they keep that night by not sleeping, but rather giving thanks and recounting the miracles and mighty deeds that Elohim performed for us on that night." "<b>Shemarim.</b> Guenosh (watching) in the vernacular. Another interpretation: <b>a night of shemarim</b> — that they keep from eating their Paschal offerings in it, in the manner of ״you shall keep, to offer it to Me in its appointed time.״"], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:57:28.451045869Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}